WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.230
So, I guess I should make 
my stance perfectly clear.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:09.820
I say...

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:18.370
Why don't we just give up 
on going to save Horizon?

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.240
What?!

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.420
Hold it! Why'd you steal my line?

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.470
'Cause the teacher said 
to "express your views",

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:40.520
but she never said who 
had to take which side.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.220
B..But...

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.890
I chose to go first because of those rules.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:47.860
There's penalties for breaking 'em.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.230
Uh...

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.010
<i>Is that the "penalty"?</i>

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:55.280
Seijun...

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.710
This could start a war 
with the Testament Union,

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:01.490
so is there any way we could
profit from saving Horizon?

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:03.730
I can't do squat.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.170
I can't answer that on my own.

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.500
So, Seijun, you tell me.

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:13.980
What exactly does my wish entail?

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.240
Nani ga mieru?

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.240
What do you see?

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.660
Ari no mama no kimi wa

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.660
You've closed yourself off to love

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:49.550
Tsuyoku naru made itoshisa wo tojite

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:49.550
Until you grow innately strong

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:52.630
Nani wo kiku no?

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:52.630
What are you listening to?

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.720
Himitsu no kobeya de

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.720
Shall I tell you about days long past

00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:01.560
Inishie no hibi katarou ka?

00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:01.560
In our secret little room?

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.770
Kioku ni dakarete

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.770
Embraced in memories

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:08.060
Kudakareta mysteria

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:08.060
The mysteria crumbles

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.820
Higeki wo koete

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.820
Once you overcome this tragedy

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:13.030
Odayaka na inori

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:13.030
Offer a gentle prayer

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:17.050
Owari ga hajimari

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:17.050
Endings are just beginnings

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:20.240
Shinsekai de hito wa mirai wo

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:20.240
People toss aside all they have

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.830
Bishu no you ni

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.830
Without ever knowing

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:26.300
Nomi hoseru ka sae shirazu

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:26.300
If they could drink up the new world

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:29.460
Subete houri nageta

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:29.460
Like a savory wine

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.620
Shinsekai wa tsumetai risei to

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.620
The new world resides

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:35.340
Kiseki no hazama

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:35.340
Between boring logic and miracles

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:44.350
Doushite koko de kimi to aeta no

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:44.350
I wonder why this is where I first met you

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:58.740
Then, let me tell you the 
merits of saving Horizon.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:00.340
Most importantly,

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:04.430
Ruler of the Land

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:02.800
it would let us secure 
Musashi's sovereign powers.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:03.570
The what?

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:06.620
<i>A country's sovereign powers 
require three attributes.</i>

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.110
<i>First, to stand as equals with other nations,</i>

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:10.710
<i>you need to display your independence.</i>

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.460
<i>Second, to keep the country standing,</i>

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:16.590
<i>someone must reign over the land and people.</i>

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:19.150
<i>Third, to support the first two,</i>

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:20.790
<i>you need the ability to make decisions.</i>

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:22.580
<i>Basically, you need ultimate authority</i>

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:24.510
<i>and command over foreign 
and internal affairs.</i>

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:28.960
<i>If you have all three,
you'll be accepted as an independent country.</i>

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:33.480
<i>At present, the Far East has lost
most of its people and land.</i>

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:37.040
And the three sovereign 
powers are being violated.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:35.980
Isn't this...

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.320
It is.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.320
Really?

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:39.350
Yes.

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.110
But if we save Horizon,

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:43.510
Musashi will obtain a Far East sovereign that

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:45.740
the Testament Union cannot touch.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:48.080
We'll preserve our sovereign powers

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.420
and stand equally with the other nations.

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:53.040
But I doubt the Testament 
Union would accept that.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:55.490
So, we'd have to go to war.

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:56.750
In that case...

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:01.800
The merchant Konishi asks:

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.760
Eh? Konishi?

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:06.120
"Even if we save the princess"

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.330
"and secure the Far East's sovereign powers,"

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:11.150
"we could still lose people to the war."

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:14.180
"What do you have to say about that?"

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:16.450
So, Seijun, your answer!

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:23.900
Aoi, did you know that there could be
a death toll even if you evade war?

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:29.330
There's a death toll even 
if we don't go to war?

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:32.510
Right, Shirojiro mentioned this earlier,

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:34.960
but if you stifle the Far East's finances,

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.960
we will eventually lose people to poverty.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:40.170
It would give rise to a death toll
created due to avoiding war.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.840
Whoa, there, just a sec.

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:46.620
So if we don't save Horizon, 
they'll conquer us,

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:48.580
and people will die even if we don't fight.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.920
But if we try to save her, we'll go to war.

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:52.530
Those are our two options.

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:54.020
In that case!

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:57.020
Politician Masanobu asks:

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:01.200
"If you want to save the princess,"

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.720
"present a valid reason for
opposing the Testament Union"

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:06.430
"aside from the issue 
regarding sovereign powers."

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:10.340
"Why do you think the Testament Union
is evil for ordering her suicide?"

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:16.280
That's a good question and request.

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:19.390
Our greatest threat is not in the Far East

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:23.710
convincing themselves that 
they are in the right.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:27.210
Rather, it lies with them convincing
the world that we are evil

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:30.220
for trying to conquer the Far East.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:35.640
Now, does he dare speak out against us?

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:39.360
Is there such a just cause?

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:42.820
"Is there some greater good in saving her?"

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:45.570
"What say you in all your inexperience?!"

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:53.290
Masazumi?

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:57.160
Uh, um, I heard a sound.

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.830
Paper... I heard paper.

00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:02.590
Masazumi brought a cheat sheet?

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:20.650
<i>What's the point in saving Horizon</i>

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:23.340
<i>and turning the Testament Union against us?</i>

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:29.320
<i>My future as a politician's 
over if I say this.</i>

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:38.040
<i>How do I even know if it will work?</i>

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:43.380
<i>He's right; it's a callow argument
from someone still green!</i>

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:47.840
Aoi?

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:52.530
Seijun, what's the point
if you don't state your own answer?!

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:53.290
But...

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:55.110
Don't give me that!

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:58.620
You're the only one amongst us
with any authority right now!

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:00.020
You're our representative!

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:02.730
So, give me your answer!

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:06.350
I...

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:07.500
Masazumi!

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:09.280
It can't be!

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.260
Divine Transmission

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:14.530
Oh, were you in the middle of something?

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:18.910
Um, I brought them, just 
like the chancellor asked.

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:21.050
Oh, go for it, Adele!

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:21.880
Okay!

00:07:23.590 --> 00:07:25.420
Masazumi!

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:26.460
Right...

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:30.530
What brought you here today?

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:31.870
Help.

00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:32.930
Help who?

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:34.790
Horizon.

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:40.070
Horizon said: Masazumi is a politician.

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:42.440
Politicians help people.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:43.930
That's...

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.000
Help, Masazumi.

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:48.440
Damn it!

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:52.360
Paper, dirty.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:55.400
That's okay, I could read it if I wanted.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:57.080
Besides...

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:58.450
You may eat it.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:03.750
You see, you've already won me over.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.400
Here's my answer.

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:13.180
There is a legitimate just cause for
rescuing Horizon Ariadust.

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:18.470
There is no need for her to take
responsibility as the ruler of Mikawa.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:23.450
Last night, Lord Motonobu died
while obliterating Mikawa.

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:25.240
But his death isn't being viewed as suicide,

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:27.860
so responsibility has shifted to his heir.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:31.740
However, Horizon was not his heiress
when Lord Motonobu died.

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:33.360
Isn't that right, Asama?

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:36.370
You got a confirmation for an
informal succession this morning.

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:38.670
Y..Yes, that's right.

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:41.120
We received notification 
via Itsukushima Shrine.

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:44.120
Horizon Ariadust does not remember her past

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.420
and has been living as a citizen of Musashi.

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:50.670
So, she was in no way related to
the destruction of Mikawa.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:54.430
<i>If they make her take responsibility
for something she had no part in,</i>

00:08:54.770 --> 00:08:58.770
<i>then the Testament Union would have
appointed someone else as heir</i>

00:08:54.770 --> 00:08:59.430
Vice-president, doesn't it seem like
he is directing this at us?

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:01.740
<i>and ordered them to commit suicide
if Horizon wasn't around.</i>

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:04.520
<i>They're taking advantage 
of reproducing history</i>

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.440
<i>to conveniently execute someone.</i>

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:08.270
<i>It's a monstrous system!</i>

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:11.340
Hold it.

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:15.030
Who's supposed to take the blame
for Mikawa's destruction?

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:18.450
Mikawa lost its ruler and 
a vast portion of land.

00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:23.460
Mikawa's citizens are living off of
Musashi's infrastructure.

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:27.120
So, you could declare Mikawa an
aerial metropolitan ship

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:29.740
and attach it to Musashi to keep it running.

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:32.170
That way we won't lose Mikawa.

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:34.380
No one has to take the blame!

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:38.010
Seriously?

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:38.010
Can they do that?

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:44.000
Divine Transmission

00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:41.940
<i>Musashi Ariadust Academy 
proposes that this is</i>

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:45.120
<i>the proper way to handle Horizon 
Ariadust and requests the</i>

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:49.020
<i>Testament Union
to reconsider their actions.</i>

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:51.990
The Testament Union is currently

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:55.150
misusing the Testament to replicate history.

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:56.960
They are disrespecting the Testament!

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:58.610
<i>That's a fallacy.</i>

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:02.660
The Pope President...

00:10:03.070 --> 00:10:04.410
<i>Tes.</i>

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:06.290
<i>Let's talk for a moment.</i>

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:11.630
Seijun, you're lookin' good!

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:13.250
Aoi, listen well.

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.850
Now for the real deal.

00:10:15.850 --> 00:10:19.540
I swear I will pave a way to Horizon.

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:26.560
You want us to release Mikawa's princess

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:29.270
since she had nothing to do with this?

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:35.560
<i>There are various interpretations on how
to recreate the Testament's history.</i>

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:39.780
<i>But these "interpretations"
are not based upon convenience.</i>

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:44.790
But Your Holiness, your interpretations will
take an innocent person's life.

00:10:45.110 --> 00:10:48.960
<i>It's martyrdom, not taking a life.</i>

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.790
<i>She's been chosen to go first,</i>

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:54.590
<i>so she can lead the people towards
the Testament's desired history.</i>

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:59.960
<i>Errors can occur when interpreting
how to reproduce history.</i>

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:02.470
<i>As such, it is necessary 
to fix those mistakes.</i>

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:04.640
He's straying from the point.

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:07.390
A normal person wouldn't notice that.

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:11.810
The Pope President is intentionally
challenging him to a debate.

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:14.100
What is the point in that?

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:17.510
No one could keep up with the vast amount of

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:19.700
opinions he's developed over the years.

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:23.180
The Pope President is reusing lines
from past experiences,

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:25.950
while his opponent must outright debate.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:29.660
His opponent will grow weary and ask to stop,

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:32.590
thus losing the debate.

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:36.750
Did you freeze our assets to "fix" an error?

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:42.380
<i>They will be automatically released
once we come to an agreement.</i>

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:45.680
Hey, hey, Seijun, you winning?

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:49.560
<i>He's applying scorched earth 
tactics to his debate.</i>

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.850
<i>The only way to break out of this is...</i>

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:54.990
It seems we hold parallel views.

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:56.790
Allow me to be frank.

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:58.510
We concede that our values are

00:11:58.510 --> 00:12:01.820
incompatible with the 
Testament Union's values.

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:05.530
I believe that even you 
would agree with me on that.

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:08.160
<i>No, I believe that we can reach a </i>

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.540
<i>mutual understanding through discussion.</i>

00:12:10.820 --> 00:12:12.060
In other words, eventually,

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:14.850
we could reach a point where our paths unite.

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:16.290
Correct?

00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:18.460
<i>Tes, exactly.</i>

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.380
That's great!

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:25.550
It means that, no matter what we do,

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.400
you believe we can talk things out peacefully

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:29.060
and eventually reach an agreement.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:31.100
Good going, Masazumi!

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:32.350
Shirojiro!

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:35.900
Prepare to gather Musashi's finances
under one management group.

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:38.140
Set it up so that Musashi 
will support all of

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:41.030
our foreign settlements that
 are suffering from frozen assets.

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:43.430
Keep the possibility of 
issuing new currency in mind.

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:45.830
If it's about money, you got it!

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:46.730
Asama!

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:47.760
BE
Inari

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:47.780
Y..Yes?

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:49.990
Issue a protest to Itsukushima Shrine

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:52.450
and request an informal 
succession reevaluation.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:55.130
Claim that anyone but Asama Shrine holding

00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:56.870
something important like this succession

00:12:56.870 --> 00:13:00.270
infringes upon your authority,
and insist on a reevaluation.

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:01.380
You got it!

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:05.480
Even I'm surprised by his far-fetched

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:07.960
take on what his Holiness said.

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:11.140
He's taking advantage of this waiting game.

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:15.290
Musashi Ariadust Academy 
will reach an understanding

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:17.980
with the Testament Union by 
maintaining three parallel points.

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:22.650
First, if the Testament Union freezes
our settlements' finances,

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:24.700
we shall inversely finance them.

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:29.160
Next, if the Testament Union declares
Horizon Ariadust the ruler

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:30.790
through that informal succession,

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:34.830
we shall inversely have an official
shrine protest and intercede.

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:37.260
<i>Finally, if the Testament 
Union tries to force </i>

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:40.010
<i>an innocent civilian to take 
the blame and commit suicide,</i>

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:43.000
<i>in order to protect Horizon 
Ariadust from your </i>

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:44.840
<i>misuse of the Testament,</i>

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:47.730
we will invite her to our academy

00:13:47.730 --> 00:13:49.170
and protect her from the

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:51.570
Testament Union as one of Musashi's students.

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:53.720
<i>What fallacy!</i>

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:55.560
<i>It's all fallacy.</i>

00:13:56.400 --> 00:14:00.110
Your Holiness, if what you said is true,

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:04.040
you have made the fallacy
and we are merely acting in parallel.

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:05.580
That's all.

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:07.530
<i>A moment, please.</i>

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:10.830
<i>You were keeping in parallel with us, right?</i>

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:13.330
<i>Then, I hate to inform you, but listen well.</i>

00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:16.500
<i>The Testament Union does not want to fight.</i>

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:19.940
<i>What is your parallel to that?</i>

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:22.520
Not good!

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:25.260
He's taking advantage 
of the parallel tactics.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:31.230
<i>We want peace, but you and 
your parallelism don't.</i>

00:14:31.230 --> 00:14:32.610
<i>What say you?</i>

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:38.110
<i>I either declare war or I admit defeat.</i>

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:39.560
<i>It's one or the other.</i>

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:43.770
<i>If you take everything back and admit defeat,</i>

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:52.720
Divine Transmission

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:46.830
<i>I shall turn a blind eye to your hostility.</i>

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:50.530
<i>I will even release your settlements' assets,</i>

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:54.990
<i>void Musashi's change in power
and let Musashi annex Mikawa.</i>

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:57.250
<i>He's compromising? But why?</i>

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:58.280
<i>Listen...</i>

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:02.580
<i>Tres España sent me a report regarding</i>

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:05.420
<i>Horizon Ariadust's Armor of Deadly Sins.</i>

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:09.820
<i>The Armor of Deadly Sins sealed
within Mikawa's princess</i>

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:12.910
<i>is called P-01s, or Oros Phthonos.</i>

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:14.590
<i>It's a new addition to the Armor </i>

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:16.920
<i>of Deadly Sins that controls "Jealousy."</i>

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:21.190
<i>Its effect is the ability to collectively
control the other Armors.</i>

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:25.240
<i>It's a master OS that can 
meld the Armors into one.</i>

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:29.090
Asama Shrine White Sand Plinth

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:29.110
<i>Recall what Motonobu, Lord of Mikawa, said?</i>

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:33.700
<i>Whoever obtains all of the Armors of Deadly Sins
can sway the apocalypse.</i>

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:37.520
<i>But why did he give his 
daughter the ability to</i>

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:39.980
<i>control them once they've been gathered?</i>

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:42.980
<i>The Testament Union believes he was</i>

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:44.960
<i>trying to conquer the Far East.</i>

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:49.370
<i>He wanted to make the nations that
possess the Armor submit to him.</i>

00:15:49.370 --> 00:15:52.130
<i>Well? Do you still wish to save the princess?</i>

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:54.790
<i>We will go to war if you do.</i>

00:15:56.510 --> 00:15:58.600
<i>We're clearly at the disadvantage.</i>

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:00.580
<i>This was fun.</i>

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:04.150
<i>You're the first one to
challenge me to a debate in ages.</i>

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:09.320
<i>Masazumi Honda,
do you want me to acknowledge our blunders</i>

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:11.870
<i>since you and your father failed to
succeed to prominent names</i>

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:14.780
<i>and your "interpretations" couldn't save you?</i>

00:16:16.480 --> 00:16:19.220
<i>After all, you were undergoing 
surgery to become</i>

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:21.530
<i>a man in pursuit of succeeding that name,</i>

00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:23.620
<i>only to ultimately fail.</i>

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:26.840
<i>You still don't have a bosom, do you?</i>

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:29.450
<i>You're a lady who dresses as a man,</i>

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:31.130
<i>unable to overcome your failed succession.</i>

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:35.140
<i>What brought you here when you need
to win the people's trust?</i>

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:38.440
<i>Even assuming no one found 
out about all your lies,</i>

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:40.600
<i>I say you're drunk with the desire to lead</i>

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:43.810
<i>and wish to oppose the claims of succession.</i>

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:48.150
I don't really care if they find out.

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:50.570
And I'm not drunk with the lust for power.

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:52.820
<i>He got me!</i>

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:56.320
<i>He thoroughly destroyed their image of me!</i>

00:16:57.030 --> 00:17:00.290
<i>No one will believe a word I say now.</i>

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:01.990
Hey, Seijun!

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:04.460
Are you seriously a chick?

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:07.520
Sweet! Checkie time!

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:19.570
Definitely a girl!

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:26.310
Nice little boobies!

00:17:26.090 --> 00:17:27.570
Aoi!

00:17:28.670 --> 00:17:30.270
Why so shy?

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:32.240
Little boobies rock!

00:17:32.240 --> 00:17:35.740
Hey, does anyone in the 
audience like flat chests?

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:37.360
I do!

00:17:37.850 --> 00:17:40.040
'Kay, I was just askin'.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:44.610
No one else fell for it!

00:17:44.610 --> 00:17:46.580
You stupid meanie!

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:50.410
Honda's over the age of 
ten, so she's too old!

00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:52.560
Don't be so bashful!

00:17:52.560 --> 00:17:55.290
Seijun has the right to 
accept or reject you too.

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:57.380
<i>More rubbish?</i>

00:17:57.650 --> 00:18:00.350
<i>Try not to stray from the subject, okay?</i>

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:02.930
Huh? Like you're one to talk!

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:05.980
I don't get a damn thing you've said so far!

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:10.320
But Seijun here found the answers
regarding what I wanna do!

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:12.410
She explained how it's actually doable!

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:17.690
I couldn't find those answers,
and neither could anyone else!

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:20.740
So, I'll support Seijun!

00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:23.160
She's the only one who gave me answers!

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:26.640
That defines my absolute evaluation of her!

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:29.190
So, I swear I will offer her...

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:30.970
and I mean her,

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:33.130
my full support in everything she said!

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:35.320
I swear I will!

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:37.410
Support, eh?

00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:42.460
<i>Someone's willing to support me
against their leader.</i>

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:45.000
And then there's you, Old Fart!

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:49.100
You've spewed out a bunch
of complaints and temptations,

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:51.710
but it all translates to "Kill Horizon!"

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:54.730
That's the only answer you've given me!

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:57.070
<i>Impossible!</i>

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:00.240
<i>Can you answer the question 
regarding the people</i>

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:02.310
<i>of Musashi and the Far East?</i>

00:19:02.310 --> 00:19:04.340
Seijun knows the answer!

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:06.060
Seijun, tell us.

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:11.220
If we rescue Horizon, is there anything
in it for the other countries?

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:16.340
Tori Aoi, let me say this first.

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:20.400
I'm sure we will clash with other nations,

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:22.890
but we must never forget 
our desire to stay alive

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:27.030
and help others survive and do
everything we can to meet those ends.

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:30.400
Everyone can prevent Horizon's death.

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:33.400
That is the first international benefit.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.150
Another benefit will come from

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:39.530
Musashi annexing Mikawa
in preparation for our just cause.

00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:43.150
Upon rescuing Horizon Ariadust,

00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:46.540
Musashi will act as the center
of sovereign power for the Far East.

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:49.040
<i>So, you're abandoning 
your foreign settlements?</i>

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:50.280
We are not.

00:19:50.280 --> 00:19:52.040
As such, Musashi hereby declares:

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:54.340
The Far East settlements shall temporarily

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:56.620
be independent self-governing cities.

00:19:56.620 --> 00:20:00.050
They will be neutral demilitarized zones.

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:02.080
And Musashi will act independently

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:04.800
as the sovereign power over the Far East.

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:08.020
<i>Why do you want sovereign powers
and escape from conquest?</i>

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:10.020
To gather the Armor of Deadly Sins

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:11.520
so we can prevent the apocalypse.

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:15.860
Musashi swears we will gather the
Armor of Deadly Sins for Horizon Ariadust,

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:19.570
endeavor to prevent the apocalypse,
and not seek compensation.

00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:23.280
In other words, we shall work to
save the world from peril.

00:20:23.590 --> 00:20:25.910
<i>You'll hold onto the WMD?!</i>

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:28.740
<i>And you think you have the right to do that?!</i>

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:29.680
We do!

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:32.990
The Armor is made from
Horizon Ariadust's stolen emotions,

00:20:32.990 --> 00:20:34.720
so they belong to her!

00:20:35.270 --> 00:20:37.530
I want any country in possession of

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:39.410
an Armor made from her stolen emotions

00:20:39.410 --> 00:20:41.220
to return them to her.

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:45.930
As representative of 
Musashi Ariadust Academy,

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:47.970
I, Masazumi Honda, hereby decree:

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:51.400
Musashi does not wish to 
war with the other nations.

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:54.220
We would like your assistance in
preventing the apocalypse.

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:57.740
But if you hinder our 
efforts to save the world,

00:20:57.740 --> 00:20:59.980
escalate the fight for 
the Armor of Deadly Sins,

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:03.990
and insist upon forcing a girl to
live without her emotions,

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:07.990
we shall use Musashi's school rules
to have the students fight...

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:10.450
and deal with you!

00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:14.420
<i>I see...</i>

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:17.040
Then, all negotiations are off.

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:19.410
We are not parallel.

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:21.960
Galileo, get her.

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:23.800
Over there!

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:28.800
I am Galileo, Vice-President 
of K.P.A. Italia.

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:33.060
Blast off!

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:36.650
Damn heretic!

00:21:40.780 --> 00:21:42.490
Could that be...

00:21:42.490 --> 00:21:44.530
You've got a keen eye.

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:49.030
[The kanji for Staseis Porneia 
means "The Lustful One."]

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:49.030
It's my country's Armor of Deadly Sins,
Staseis Porneia.

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:53.690
It's on loan, but I can use it well enough
to fight on a personal level.

00:21:54.110 --> 00:21:59.290
Its ability is to "renounce and play
with any power it touches."

00:21:59.290 --> 00:22:00.040
Go!

00:22:04.810 --> 00:22:06.880
You have rather weak punches.

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:07.470
What?!

00:22:07.750 --> 00:22:09.220
Ptolemaic Theory!

00:22:17.280 --> 00:22:18.570
Teleportation?!

00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:21.230
So, it's finally come to this, 
Representative of Musashi.

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:24.780
Your little debate back 
there was rather amusing.

00:22:24.780 --> 00:22:27.990
I'd say class is now adjourned.

00:22:41.210 --> 00:22:43.050
I am Colonel of the Mikawa Guard,

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:45.620
Futayo Honda!

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:50.260
Our voyage across the real world

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:50.260
Sora ni nozomu you ni

00:22:50.540 --> 00:22:57.270
Koukai suru genjitsu sekai no tabi

00:22:50.540 --> 00:22:57.270
Is like navigating straight for the sky

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:01.610
Nani mo mottenai kedo

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:01.610
I may not have anything

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.720
Kokoro no naka

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.720
But I have a dream

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:08.950
Kagayaita yume ga aru yo

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:08.950
That's shone brightly in my heart

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.790
Mada kikoenai

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.790
I still haven't heard

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:15.280
Kimi no hontou no mune no koe

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:15.280
The voice spoken from your heart

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:20.200
Shiritain da — sugao wo misete yo

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:20.200
Let me in — show me the real you

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:23.790
Barabara ni chirabatta

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:23.790
We'll bury the void

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:26.890
Ikutsu mo no piisu wo

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:26.890
As we find all of the pieces

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:29.560
Hitotsu zutsu sagashite

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:29.560
That have gotten scattered around

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:32.720
Kuuhaku wo umete iku no sa

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:32.720
One piece at a time

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:37.540
Ubawareta kimi no egao

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:37.540
Your smile has been stolen

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:41.210
Tori modosu tame ni hashiru yo

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:41.210
But I will race to get it back

00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:47.150
Boku wa hikari sasu michi wo

00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:47.150
As I run down the shining path

00:24:07.150 --> 00:24:10.990
Next Episode
The Summit's Flower
